{
  "title": "Build shopping list categorization golden test set from prod data",
  "description": "Shopping list categorization \
(ramekin-core/src/ingredient_categorizer.rs, data/ingredients.json) has no \
quality measurement against real usage. We want a golden test set built from \
actual historical shopping list items on the prod server.\n\
\n\
This issue is intended to be worked ON THE PROD SERVER (it needs read access \
to the prod database). Everything is soft-deleted, never hard-deleted, so the \
shopping_list_items table contains the full history of every item ever added.\n\
\n\
Steps:\n\
1. Extract distinct item strings with usage counts from prod: roughly `SELECT \
item, COUNT(*) FROM shopping_list_items GROUP BY item ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC` \
(include soft-deleted rows; that's the point). These are post-parsing item \
names plus hand-typed manual entries — the real input distribution the \
categorizer sees.\n\
2. Commit the corpus to the repo as a data file (e.g. \
data/shopping-list-items.txt, one `count<TAB>item` per line), following the \
spirit of data/unique-ingredients.txt. This is a single-user personal server, \
so committing the item names is fine.\n\
3. Produce a labeled golden set for the most frequent items (e.g. top 500-1000 \
by count): expected category for each, using the 16 categories in \
ingredient_categorizer.rs. LLM-draft the labels, then have a human review iffy \
ones. Store as a data file (e.g. data/shopping-list-category-golden.json).\n\
4. Add a test/make target (pattern: the existing ingredient-tests-* targets in \
the Makefile) that runs the categorizer over the golden set and reports \
frequency-weighted accuracy and the 'Other' rate, failing or reporting on \
regressions.\n\
\n\
Context: replicating the matcher over data/unique-ingredients.txt (16,411 \
recipe-derived ingredient strings) gives a ~10.7% 'Other' rate, but that \
corpus is recipe-derived and includes parse junk. The prod corpus is the \
ground truth for what actually lands on shopping lists.\n\
\n\
Follow-up issue p2-expand-ingredient-categorizer-keywords.json5 will use this \
golden set to drive keyword expansion.",
  "status": "open",
